WEBVTT

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:33.500
[laughing]

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.860
[chuckles] Oh!

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.220
[spitting]

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:59.860
[Lightning] Wow. What is this place?

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:01.940
Wheel Well.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:05.260
Used to be the most popular stop
on the mother road.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.660
This place?

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.700
[horns beeping]

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.340
[Sally sighing] Yeah, imagine.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:21.700
Oh, imagine what
it must have been like to stay here.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.620
You know, I don't get you.

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:28.940
How does a Porsche
wind up in a place like this?

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:31.180
Well, it's really pretty simple.
I was...

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.420
...an attorney in LA
livin' life in the fast lane, and...

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:39.060
Oh, you were, were you?
Were you rich?

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:42.500
- What?
- Just... clues to the puzzle.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.940
Yeah, OK.
Well, that was my life.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:47.780
And you know what?

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:51.500
It never felt... happy.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:56.180
Yeah. I mean... really?

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.020
Yeah. So I left California.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:01.380
Just drove and drove
and finally broke down right here.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:04.900
Doc fixed me up, Flo took me in.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:08.020
Well, they all did. And I never left.

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:10.980
Yeah. You know, I understand.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.900
You need a little R and R.
Recharge the old batteries.

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:17.700
But you know, after a while,
why didn't you go back?

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:22.100
[inhaling heavily] I fell in love.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:25.860
- Oh.
- Yep.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:29.500
- Corvette?
- No.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:37.780
I fell in love with this.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:53.540
Whoa. Look at that.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:56.740
Look, they're drivin' right by.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:59.020
They don't even know
what they're missing!

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:02.340
[Sally] Well,
it didn't used to be that way.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:05.140
Oh, yeah?

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:09.100
Yeah. Forty years ago,
that Interstate down there didn't exist.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:11.260
Really?

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:14.020
[Sally] Yeah. Back then,

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.940
cars came across the country
a whole different way.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:19.580
How do you mean?

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:23.020
The road didn't cut through the land
like that Interstate.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:27.300
It moved with the land, you know?
It rose, it fell, it curved.

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:30.780
- Mornin'!
- Nice day, huh?

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:35.500
Cars didn't drive on it
to make great time.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:38.140
They drove on it to have a great time.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:40.340
[♪ James Taylor: Our Town]

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.540
Well, what happened?

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:18.100
The town got bypassed
just to save ten minutes of driving.

